{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791366596,"nonce":"G5sVoTMB3ShuhQT9aYC2fb6XoEA=","message":"Implemented bounded, memoized known-bits analysis in the shared HIR constant folder. It derives integer facts from AND/OR/XOR, NOT, select-arm intersections, truncation and integer extensions/bitcasts. Facts are masked to 8/16/32/64/128-bit widths. Eq/Ne fold only when bits prove equality or a contradiction. Unknown definitions, loads, phis, pointer casts and float conversions remain unknown. Recursive analysis is bounded to 16 levels. Only comparisons are removed; operand producers remain for their effects. No frontend, tiering-threshold or Wasmtime dependency changes.\n\nZYNTAX_DISABLE_KNOWN_BITS=1 safely disables the pass for A/B diagnosis. Benchmark runs below disable LLVM entirely while retaining interpreter-first tiering and Cranelift promotion.\n\nNative evidence (Mac ARM64, final executable, switch off/on): Lua NBody.advance VCode falls from 1333 to 1110 lines, floating-point selects from 41 to 26. The nearby OR-by-4 / compare-with-3 pairs disappear; energy remains -169096. Artifacts: /tmp/zyntax-known-bits-final-{off,on}.ir and .out. These are code inspections, not Mac benchmark claims.\n\nNUC method: shared benchmark lock, CPU affinity 0-7, alternating independent processes, LLVM disabled and both binaries verified as cranelift. Baseline is 7c4ab6da47df59d88e1cd778664262785ff0985a; final candidate includes the disable switch. Existing desktop/HUD processes remained running. All 17 Lua and 22 supported Python kernel outputs/checksums pass. pidigits remains unsupported. Wall measurements include the full process; kernel values use the harness reporting.\n\nFinal baseline/candidate Lua medians, five runs per arm:\n\n| Kernel | Kernel before ms | Kernel after ms | Wall before ms | Wall after ms |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| fib | 12.95 | 12.88 | 35.46 | 35.90 |\n| binary_trees 